  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Who wins",
      "items": [
        "Each step checks the body first: lifted, then the desk's edge, then a long touch, then faces (guardian.py 152–193). From any state, a lift or an edge comes first; the diagram draws those from Guarding only.",
        "Both ground sensors over nothing counts as lifted, so a head-on edge stops the robot rather than backing it off (guardian.py 87–92)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Friends are numbers",
      "items": [
        "The owner card shown with a face makes that face's number a friend; without familiar, the face in view is a friend until it has been gone 10 s (guardian.py 140–149).",
        "When the phone forgets its faces (familiar off, another page or phone), the guardian forgets its friends too: the numbers may go to someone else (guardian_node.py 74–80)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "One brain, three worlds",
      "items": [
        "It reads only topics (guardian_node.py 96–129): guardian_check plays it with a mock phone and a fake Thymio, scripts/guardian_twin_check.py on the Thymio twin in Webots, ./start.sh --guardian with the real phone."
      ]
    }
  ]
